    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the codebase's existing conventions for owner fields.\n\n**What the change does:** Owners now accept an optional `title` (e.g. `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`) on create, and expose a computed read-only `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n**Changes made, each in the layer where it belongs:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added `title` as an optional editable string on `OwnerFields` (the request/input schema, alongside `firstName`/`lastName`).\n   - Added `salutation` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` response schema, matching the pattern of the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, \u2026).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (domain model):\n   - Added the persisted `title` column with a standard getter/setter.\n   - Added `getSalutation()` as a `@Transient` derived accessor next to the sibling `getDisplayName()` \u2014 a small, single-responsibility method that reuses the inherited `getLastName()`.\n\n3. **Schema DDL** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`): added the `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (the test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column is required there).\n\nMapStruct wires everything automatically by name: `title` from the DTO into `Owner.setTitle`, and `Owner.getSalutation()` into the response DTO \u2014 no mapper edits needed, consistent with how `displayName`/`initials` already work.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 `\"DR who\"`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
